  "worked_solution": "First, we factor the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}\u2061\\theta -\\operatorname{tan}\u2061\\theta {sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta }{2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta \\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta } & =\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}\u2061\\theta (1-{sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta )}{2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta \\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we rewrite the numerator using $1-{sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta ={cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta $ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}\u2061\\theta (1-{sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta )}{2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta \\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta } & =\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}\u2061\\theta {cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta }{2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta \\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}\u2061\\theta \\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta \\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }}{2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta \\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}\u2061\\theta \\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }{2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}\u2061\\theta \\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }{2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we rewrite $\\operatorname{tan}\u2061\\theta $ using its definition and simplify further:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}\u2061\\theta \\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }{2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta } & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }{2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta }}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }{2\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta }} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }}\\cdot \\frac{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}\u2061\\theta -\\operatorname{tan}\u2061\\theta {sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta }{2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta \\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }=\\frac{1}{2}\n$$",
